//
// Host-only self-test of the GGUF q4_0 codec (synthetic payload, no
// checkpoint, no device; leg (d) imports matvec_int4_packed, so `air` must be
// importable). Collected by the unfiltered check-programming-examples only.
//
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/gguf_q4_0.py --self-test | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: [a] q4_0 block split (d, qs): PASS (512 blocks)
// CHECK: [b] q4_0 nibble un-interleave: PASS (16384 nibbles)
// CHECK: [c] repack -> kernel Q convention: PASS
// CHECK: [d] cpu_reference(repack) vs direct q4_0 dequant: PASS
// CHECK: [e] negative control (skip un-interleave): correctly DIFFERS on {{[1-9][0-9]*}} / 16384 nibbles
// CHECK: [f] llama_unpermute_rows inverts llama.cpp's RoPE permute: PASS
// CHECK: [g] un-permute moves Q rows and S/Z together: PASS
// CHECK: [k] q4_1 block split + exact `d*q + m` dequant: PASS
// CHECK: [l] quantise-from-source beats transcode-from-q4_1: PASS (rms {{[0-9.e-]+}} < {{[0-9.e-]+}})
// CHECK: [m] promoted tensor without reference: correctly REFUSED
// CHECK: [n] quantize_q4_0 == quantize_row_q4_0_ref bytes: PASS ({{[0-9]+}} blocks; the fp16-reciprocal rule differs on {{[1-9][0-9]*}})
// CHECK: All self-tests PASSED.
